// §14 entry 15 -- refcount saturation -> a RUNTIME ABORT, not wraparound.
// Different SHAPE from almost every other entry: this is not a compile
// rejection at all.
//
// §6.5: "64-bit on every target, including ilp32, saturating with hard
// abort. A 32-bit refcount overflows at 2^32, which is reachable --
// CVE-2016-0728 (Linux keyring) is exactly this, overflow -> UAF -> local
// root. RISC-V ilp32 is in scope; the target's word size does not get to
// choose." §6.6: "Destructor resurrection -- re-referencing an object under
// destruction -- aborts."
//
// Retaining a `refero<T>` 2^64 times is not something a written loop can
// reach (that is the whole point of the saturating design -- it is
// deliberately astronomically far from any workload this project can spend
// wall-clock time driving to), so the realistic version of this fixture,
// once it can run at all, is a program built with a debug/test hook that
// fast-forwards a refcount to `UINT64_MAX - 1` and then performs ONE more
// retain -- not a `dum ... terminus 2^64` loop, which §8.5 could not even
// parse today regardless (control flow is `[OPEN]`, design-only). The loop
// below is written as the honest, ordinary-source shape of "keep retaining
// this value" for readability; it is explicitly NOT how the real
// conformance check would be driven once one exists.
//
// DEFERRED, and the blocker is NOT the ARC runtime. That half of this header
// was false: `exsrt_retain` in compiler/x86_64/prelude/prelude.asm saturates
// by construction -- `add qword [rdi + EXS_OBJ_RC], 1` followed by `jc
// exsrt_abort_saturatio` -- and `rc == 0` means UNDER DESTRUCTION, so §6.6's
// resurrection is one compare; tests/unit/prelude_arc.asm exercises both,
// including the `abortus 2` line on fd 2 and exit 132. The saturating
// refcount is built.
//
// THE BLOCKER IS THAT NO SOURCE PROGRAM CAN HOLD A `refero` VALUE. `refero<T>`
// has a grammar production (6f6cd8c) and a type, and nothing constructs one:
// `grep -rl refero tests/programs examples` is empty, and the prelude's
// `alloc` row yields an ARENA, not a reference. So there is no program to
// build, with or without a hook, and `needs=refero_construction` says so.
// (A debug hook that fast-forwarded a refcount from outside the language
// would be either an environment read CLAUDE.md forbids or a new language
// surface -- neither is a thing this fixture may invent.)
//
// A second thing is also missing and is not the gate: tests/run.sh has no
// `abort` shape implementation, so nothing would recognise the
// SIGILL/`abortus N` shape if it fired. That branch is a grading rule over a
// program that exists; this entry has no program yet.

// `dum COND { ... }` is §8.5's own attested shape (`dum COND terminus N`);
// the condition spelling and an unbounded `dum` with no `terminus` are
// both themselves outside what §8.5 settles (control flow is "[OPEN]
// Design only" in full, and `certus` rule 6 wants every loop bounded
// besides) -- `verum` here is illustrative prose, not an attested boolean
// literal; none exists in any spec section read for this suite.
publica functio satura(n: refero<mensura>) poscit alloc {
    dum verum {
        n.retine();
    }
}

// TEST: entry=15 shape=abort status=deferred needs=refero_construction
